{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"5853104f44b46f2542da9dc80a614770ed1c86560698bf82406fbf4fd5652a24","packTokens":2575,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":240,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":698,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1316,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using their Folio3 Google account, with employee profiles and vehicle details populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking with a single action and view its status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can schedule or cancel parking releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can view availability and claim released parking on a first-come, first-served basis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and generate and email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"When an employee with multiple registered vehicles claims temporary parking, which vehicle's plate should be authorized for that day's allocation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The employee selects one registered vehicle when claiming; only that plate is authorized for the allocation.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which timezone defines “today,” the 30-day scheduling window, the daily release time, and Monday-morning report scheduling?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the office's local timezone for all date boundaries and scheduled times.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the system choose the assigned parking floor when it automatically allocates a claimed space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Choose a floor with the most remaining capacity, using a consistent tie-break when floors are equally available.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Which sources should provide the employee, vehicle, and parking-assignment records, and how should existing records be loaded?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the corporate directory for employee identity and an administrator-maintained parking/vehicle roster for assignments, initially loaded from existing records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How long should release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history be retained?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply Folio3's existing records-retention policy to these histories.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"If a dedicated holder arrives in a vehicle with a permanent parking sticker after releasing their space and another employee has claimed it, which access outcome should apply?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Honor the permanent sticker holder's entry; the temporary claimant may be denied if the released space is occupied.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Which dates count as working days for the default dedicated-parking availability and related utilization scenarios?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat Monday through Friday as working days, without excluding holidays.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"What parking information should security guards be able to access beyond the indicator result at the entrance?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only use the indicator; do not provide guards with a product screen or parking records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Restrict sign-in to Folio3 Google Workspace accounts, show returning employees their dashboard, and retrieve employee profiles by corporate email with directory details and administrator-maintained parking and vehicle roster data, including an initial roster load.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"For employees without dedicated parking, require at least one registered license plate before claims are enabled; support multiple plates with optional make, model, and color, and make each newly registered plate immediately eligible.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Treat Monday through Friday, including holidays, as working days for default dedicated-parking availability and utilization.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Let dedicated parking holders release today's space in one action, reject duplicate or ineligible releases, and show whether the space is Reserved, Released, or Claimed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Allow dedicated holders to schedule releases up to 30 calendar days ahead, display saved releases on a calendar, allow cancellation only before a space is claimed, and record scheduling and cancellation events.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Set the default daily release time to 8:00 AM and let administrators configure it in the office's local timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Use the configured office-local timezone to evaluate today, scheduling windows, release cutoffs, and weekly report scheduling.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Make scheduled releases and same-day releases available at the daily release time, and make same-day releases submitted after that time available immediately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Show available-space counts and allocate each available space to the first eligible non-dedicated employee whose claim is accepted, allowing each space to be claimed only once.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Require temporary parking claimants to select one registered vehicle, authorize only its plate, and assign the floor with the most remaining capacity using a consistent tie-break.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"When spaces become available, email eligible employees without dedicated parking using a fixed-template message.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Reject employee cancellation of temporary parking claims in Phase 1.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"For car-plate detections from the existing entrance LPR camera, verify temporary allocation for the office-local date and activate the green indicator only for valid authorization; return no parking authorization result or indicator call for non-car objects.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Record permanent-sticker vehicle detections for utilization, bypass temporary authorization and entry blocking for those detections, and limit guard-facing access to the indicator result alone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"For camera, recognition, network, or indicator failures, or unreadable plates, issue no automatic green authorization and record an unsuccessful verification result for manual handling.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Record Unused Dedicated Parking for each working day when a dedicated holder did not release the space and no registered vehicle entry was detected, and Unused Temporary Parking when a claimant's selected vehicle was not detected entering on the claim date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Generate a weekly utilization report every Monday morning in the office timezone, including unused dedicated and temporary parking lists, daily and weekly statistics, released-space and temporary-claim totals, and overall utilization percentage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Email each weekly report to designated stakeholders using the configured recipient list, and reflect administrator updates to that list in the next report email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Do not create automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on parking utilization in Phase 1.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Retain release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history according to Folio3's existing records-retention policy.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Deliver one responsive web app for phone, tablet, and desktop, avoiding horizontal overflow and using touch-sized controls on narrow layouts; support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Conform main flows to WCAG 2.1 AA; provide English, left-to-right content only, light mode only, and require an online connection for parking flows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Support the assumed employee and record population during the first year of deployment.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}